id: pm-gh1580
title: "GH-1580: Host-bound extension settings sections"
description: "SDK: no supported reader for an extension's own settings section, so packages re-read settings.json by path and lose their configuration on non-filesystem backends"
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: configuration,extensions,"gh:1580",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-25T00:09:23.381Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T18:26:58.428Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:41.909Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T12:21:41.909Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: SDK-owned settings-section read and revision-safe write primitives on host-bound extension contexts; backend-neutral capability/refusal contracts; avoid direct settings.json reads.
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "New public readSettingsSection, writeSettingsSection and settingsSectionRevision (core/store/settings-sections.ts) plus host-bound context.sdk.readSettingsSection and writeSettingsSection; revision-safe compare-and-set via expectedRevision; typed refusals settings_section_name_invalid, settings_section_reserved (core keys derived from the validator shape), settings_section_document_malformed, settings_section_invalid, settings_section_revision_conflict and settings_section_document_missing; writes keep every other key and record one settings:section:write history event. Documented in docs/SDK_CONFIGURATION_SAFETY.md."
expected_result: "Extensions read and validate their own settings through host-bound SDK services with typed capability/refusal and revision evidence, without reading settings.json by path."
actual_result: "16 section specs pass at 100% module coverage: stored/default reads with revisions, validator refusals, malformed documents, reserved and invalid names, add/replace/remove with history, unchanged no-op, stale compare-and-set refusal, non-JSON values, uninitialized tracker, public export identity and context.sdk binding."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
